Mock PDF content for History: World War I Timeline.
Key Events:
- Assassination of Archduke Franz Ferdinand (June 28, 1914)
- Outbreak of War and Triple Entente vs. Central Powers (August 1914)
- Battle of the Somme and Gallipoli Campaign (1915-1916)
- Entry of the United States (April 1917)
- Armistice Day (November 11, 1918)
- Treaty of Versailles (1919)
